  "limitations": [
    "Fixed membership of 1..64 voters and caller-trusted peer identities; no authentication or dynamic voter/directory handling.",
    "Leader role is an election result, not a lease or commit permission; replication owner must detect quorum loss and call lose_quorum.",
    "observe_leader provides local term/identity fencing, not standalone remote-election proof. Actual histories only supply previously elected leaders.",
    "Caller-confirmed positive term/index summaries, empty (0,0), do not validate content or represent Kafka nonempty epoch-zero logs, reconcile/truncate data, replicate or track commit.",
    "Checked u64 term/index domain differs from signed Kafka wire epoch/offset domains; no pre-vote or Vote/Begin/End RPC/API advertisement.",
    "Positive bounded caller-clock timeouts and deterministic PRNG are scheduler primitives; no cryptographic randomness, uniform-distribution or real-time performance qualification.",
    "Snapshot budget includes initialization, maximum 65,536; full-state journal has no automatic compaction, and exhaustion poisons until recovery.",
    "Injected private store isolates ambiguous election persistence consequences; physical power loss remains unqualified.",
    "Reuse Journal synchronous dedicated-thread requirement, process-local ownership guard, caller cross-process exclusivity, CRC corruption-only detection and Linux overlayfs validation limits.",
    "Finite 16-seed histories, Apache source references and 13 passing election tests do not establish full KRaft compatibility or production qualification.",
